00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:24,720
Beginning our series on soteriology, which is just fancy theological term for the study of salvation.

2
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:27,980
Soteria, meaning salvation, that's the Greek word for salvation.

3
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,220
And logi, meaning study.

4
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:32,860
Alright, and we want to address something very important.

5
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:37,580
One of the most frequently asked questions amongst believers.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:42,780
People want to know, are infants and mentally disabled people guilty?

7
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:51,020
You see, theologically this is predicated on your understanding of a key theological concept called original sin.

8
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:57,410
And just in case you're hearing that for the first time, it is predicated on your understanding of Romans chapter 5, verse 12.

9
00:00:57,810 --> 00:01:01,570
However, you may understand it, but this is what Romans 5:12 says.

10
00:01:01,730 --> 00:01:12,530
It says, therefore, just as through one man sin entered into the world, and death through sin, and therefore death spread on all men, because all have sinned.

11
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:14,210
Now pay attention to verse 14.

12
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:24,120
It says, nevertheless, death reigned from Adam to Moses, even over those who had not sinned according to the likeness of the transgression of Adam.

13
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:38,560
So the understanding of death passing on all men, even those who had not sinned according to the similitude of Adam, gave people the understanding that the guilt of Adam.

14
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,640
Now pay attention to the choice of words.

15
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:44,280
The guilt of Adam has been passed on all men.

16
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:52,560
And so even before you commit any sin, as long as you're born a sinner.

17
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,520
People have different understandings of this.

18
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:03,359
Some people nuance the differentiation between the noun and the verb.

19
00:02:03,359 --> 00:02:07,800
And by this they mean I sinned because I'm a sinner.

20
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:08,400
Okay?

21
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:18,730
So if you understand this, I mean, if you understand original sin that way, then the answer is yes.

22
00:02:19,290 --> 00:02:27,530
Children who are born and maybe die in their infancy as sinners, and so they go where sinners go.

23
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:38,050
And people who are maybe mentally challenged and then are not in a position to even hear and believe the gospel, are going to go to hell.

24
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:39,450
But here is what you need to know.

25
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:52,420
And a lot of brilliant scholars have pointed out that clearly In Romans chapter 5, verse 12, it is death that passed on all men, not sin.

26
00:02:52,580 --> 00:03:03,620
Now some go to the other extreme and there is a theological heresy, you know, where they say you didn't receive any consequence of Adam's sin.

27
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:16,010
That is not what is being said here, but what is really actually being received, take note, is I will add the propensity to eventually sin, all right?

28
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:22,170
And specifically, as highlighted in Romans 5, death, specifically.

29
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:23,330
And so what does it say?

30
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:26,010
It says, therefore through one man, sin entered into the world.

31
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:32,490
And death through sin, it says, and death, what spread to all men?

32
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:33,250
Death.

33
00:03:33,970 --> 00:03:37,250
Death spread to all men because all have sinned.

34
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:40,210
So that's what is really said here.

35
00:03:40,290 --> 00:03:46,210
And you see, I was listening to two theologians as they grappled with this concept and they gave me strong points.

36
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:50,490
And I want to mention their names and just tell you so that you can follow their line of thought.

37
00:03:50,490 --> 00:03:51,890
Michael Heiser is the first one.

38
00:03:51,890 --> 00:03:53,730
He said something very profound.

39
00:03:55,250 --> 00:04:12,780
If you have the blanket understanding of original sin and you think that everyone who is born is a sinner simply because they are born through the lineage of Adam, it means even if Jesus never committed any sin, he is a sinner.

40
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:17,899
And a lot of theologians have a cop out of that argument.

41
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:20,459
And they say, well, the virgin birth.

42
00:04:20,459 --> 00:04:26,550
Jesus was born of a virgin, and that exonerates him from the sinful tendencies of the first Adam.

43
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:29,990
I thought that before I preached that for many years.

44
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:33,270
But then he threw a curveball at me.

45
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:41,190
And then he said, well, who says that the sin is only transmitted through the man and not the woman?

46
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:49,110
Even if Jesus was not born by the man seed, that's by Joseph's seed.

47
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:50,180
Guess what?

48
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,100
A woman carried him.

49
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:54,780
And even biologically, you share the attributes of a woman.

50
00:04:54,860 --> 00:05:06,540
So are you saying that the Holy Ghost just blew earth into Mary's fetus, or did Mary actually participate in the conception?

51
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:14,420
In fact, he argued that the Catholics actually understood the problem of this implication.

52
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:19,910
And that's why they had to circle back and say, hey, Mary is also sinless, okay?

53
00:05:19,910 --> 00:05:27,150
Because they knew, you know, it's not going to work by just saying, hey, because he didn't partake of Joseph, therefore he's sinless.

54
00:05:27,150 --> 00:05:32,070
So they had to use that defense and say Mary is also sinless, which is not biblical.

55
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:33,190
The Bible doesn't say that.

56
00:05:33,269 --> 00:05:33,830
Okay?

57
00:05:34,790 --> 00:05:38,950
The simple answer for why Jesus did not commit sin was that Jesus is God.

58
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:41,910
You know, that's simple answer.

59
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:49,840
And you have to understand, the Bible didn't categorically tell us that the reason why Jesus did not commit sin is because he was born a virgin.

60
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,640
It just seemed like a plausible reason.

61
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:55,440
And a lot of theologians went with that.

62
00:05:55,600 --> 00:06:03,040
But when you think about the fact that he also partook of Mary as well, then that throws it under the bus.

63
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:13,230
So it won't be enough that Jesus committed no sin if every human who is born is automatically a sinner.

64
00:06:13,470 --> 00:06:14,030
All right?

65
