73
00:07:19,499 --> 00:07:27,340
Assuredly, I say to you, unless you are converted and you become like little children, you will by no means enter the kingdom of heaven.

74
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,500
Therefore, whoever humbles himself, yeah.

75
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:36,040
So humility, yeah, is the metaphoric idea, but it's deeper than that, as these little children is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven.

76
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:46,480
Whoever receives one little child like this in my name, whoever receives one little child like this one in my name receives me.

77
00:07:46,559 --> 00:07:59,020
And whoever causes one of these little ones to stumble, little ones who believe in me to sin, it is better for him to put a millstone to.

78
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:05,970
So Jesus places premium, you know, on this little one, and implicitly.

79
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:12,130
This is William Len Criggs, and this is, by the way, professor of theology and philosophy.

80
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:12,610
All right?

81
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:13,570
And then he.

82
00:08:13,570 --> 00:08:24,850
He's saying, at least Jesus will be careful enough not to make a juxtaposition of children in reference to entering the kingdom if they were also on that gift.

83
00:08:24,850 --> 00:08:25,490
Do you understand?

84
00:08:26,210 --> 00:08:28,570
And I will just add and throw in my own.

85
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:38,770
When you see what Jesus preached, first and foremost from the popular John 3:16, For God to love the world, he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believes in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.

86
00:08:39,169 --> 00:08:41,090
In verse 18, what does he say?

87
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:52,370
Whoever believes in him is not condemned, but he who does not believe is condemned already because he has not believed in the name of the Only Begotten Son.

88
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:56,270
And this is the condemned condemnation, verse 19.

89
00:08:56,270 --> 00:09:03,270
And this is the condemnation that light has come into the world and men love darkness, meaning this is the dividing line.

90
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:23,590
So if I'm running with this assumption, it means for this kind of condemnation, the way Jesus explained it to come upon you must have come to what theologians call the age of accountability and age where you are old enough to hear the Gospel, assimilate it, and then choose whether to accept or to reject it.

91
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:24,310
All right?

92
00:09:24,710 --> 00:09:32,710
So the condemnation comes to those who hear the gospel, understand it, but choose not to receive it.

